Z||000000||BRIAN CORNELIUS||03-21-2000||08:45 PM||||When swaping a v-6 for the 4 cylinder fiero engine the question that I hope someone can answer is: does the computer need to be also replaced? and are there any things that deserve special attention? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||pherder||03-21-2000||09:02 PM||||The things I can think of off hand are:<P>ECM,<BR>Engine wiring (and if you have an 84, ENTIRE wiring harness in the car)<BR>fuel pump,<BR>depending on what year your Fiero is:  fuel lines,<BR>??<P>Ran out of thoughts.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||BRIAN CORNELIUS||03-21-2000||09:31 PM||||The Fiero is an '88 so I was hoping the computer would be upgraded to handle the v-6. Is the fuel pump need because it is a higher pressure? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||03-21-2000||10:31 PM||||The ECMs are different part numbers. (not to mention the chip differences.)<P>Fuel pressure for MPFI (V6) is 45# where the TBI (L4) it is 15#<P>A V6 will idle with the L4's fuel pump but will not get enough fuel to run above an idle.<P>Paul<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||03-21-2000||11:52 PM||||Nope, it won't even idle.||||reg||1
